  "explanation": "The model missed a US hospitalization peak likely because additional seeding from contemporaneous southern-hemisphere influenza activity was not represented. The minimal change is to add an exogenous importation driver that increases local transmission risk when external incidence/travel from affected regions is high. Using a travel importation pressure signal (rather than directly coupling to a specific country time series) is the smallest mechanism edit that captures the effect of southern-hemisphere outbreaks seeding cases that elevate US hospitalizations.",
  "proposed_edit_type": "add_exogenous_importation_driver",
